---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Savelope"
  description="How Savelope handles your data: what stays on your device, what the app measures, and which third-party services are involved."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="prose--meta">Last updated: {SITE.lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        Savelope is built by Mihails Kuznecovs. This policy explains what the app does with
        your information in plain language. The short version: your challenges and savings
        data are yours, they live on your device and in your own iCloud account, and the
        developer cannot read them.
      </p>

      <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Everything you create in Savelope — your challenges, envelope amounts, the envelopes
        you have opened, your notes, themes and settings — is stored locally on your device.
        If you enable iCloud, this data syncs through <strong>Apple CloudKit</strong> into
        your own private iCloud container. It is governed by{' '}
        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" rel="noopener">Apple's privacy policy</a>,
        and the developer has no access to its contents.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you share a challenge with another person, the challenge data you choose to share
        is shared through CloudKit with the people you invite, and only with them.
      </p>

      <h2>What the app measures</h2>
      <p>
        Savelope collects anonymous usage and diagnostic information to understand which
        features people use and to find crashes. This includes things like which screens are
        opened, which actions are taken, app version, device model and operating system
        version. It is not used to identify you and is not sold.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>Savelope uses the following services, each with its own privacy policy:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Firebase</strong> — analytics and crash diagnostics.{' '}
          <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" rel="noopener">Privacy policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>TelemetryDeck</strong> — privacy-focused product analytics.{' '}
          <a href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/" rel="noopener">Privacy policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>RevenueCat</strong> — manages subscriptions and purchase status.{' '}
          <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy/" rel="noopener">Privacy policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Apple CloudKit &amp; the App Store</strong> — sync, sharing and payments.{' '}
          <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" rel="noopener">Privacy policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Unsplash</strong> — only if you choose a photo background for a custom
          theme; your search terms are sent to Unsplash to return results.{' '}
          <a href="https://unsplash.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Privacy policy</a>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Payments</h2>
      <p>
        Savelope is free to download with an optional Premium subscription. All purchases are
        processed by Apple. The developer never sees or stores your payment card, billing
        address or Apple Account credentials — only whether a subscription is currently
        active.
      </p>

      <h2>Notifications</h2>
      <p>
        If you turn on daily reminders, those notifications are scheduled locally on your
        device. You can turn them off at any time in the app or in iOS Settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Savelope is rated 4+ and is not directed at children under 13, and the developer does
        not knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a child has
        provided personal information, please get in touch and it will be deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Deleting the app removes the data stored on your device.</li>
        <li>
          Data synced to iCloud can be removed in iOS Settings under your Apple Account →
          iCloud → Manage Account Storage.
        </li>
        <li>
          You can limit ad and analytics identifiers in iOS Settings → Privacy &amp; Security
          → Tracking.
        </li>
        <li>
          To request information or deletion, email{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        This policy may be updated as the app changes. Material changes will be reflected here
        with a new "last updated" date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy? Email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
